# Reflection on Workplace Etiquette Assessment

## Situation
I undertook an assessment on workplace etiquette, which covered topics such as handling rude emails, punctuality for meetings, 
managing confidential information, and appropriate use of personal devices at work.

## Task
My aim was to prove that I understand the unwritten rules of professional conduct in an office environment. 
This involved knowing how to respond appropriately to difficult situations and demonstrating respect for colleagues and company policies.

## Action
I studied the guidelines on professional behavior provided in the course. 
I thought critically about each scenario presented in the quiz, 
such as what to do if you receive a rude email or how to handle confidential data. 
I applied the principle of professionalism: remaining calm, respectful, and solution-oriented in all interactions. 
I also reinforced the importance of arriving early for meetings and keeping personal device usage to a minimum during work hours.

## Result
I earned a perfect score of 100%. This achievement shows that I have a strong grasp of workplace etiquette.
I now feel prepared to navigate the social and professional norms of any workplace. 
I know how to maintain professionalism under pressure, protect sensitive information, 
and contribute positively to a respectful and productive work environment.
